Z||000035||Wade87GT||11-18-2001||11:12 PM||||Jay, from SUPERCAR CLASSICS magazine (Sept 1988) "...anyone who had the slightest chance to have a Ferrari in his life and passed it up was a fool". I bought a really nice 1982 Mondial coupe back in 1993 (not to avoid being a fool, but YOU know) for $22,000. Six and a half memorable years later I had to sell it (divorce). That was 2 1/2 years ago and I remember as it went down the road, with its new owner, like it was yesterday. That guy got a steal for $17,500. So listen to yourself because most people do not understand the obsession unless they get bit by it themselves. But I'll add some text anyway. GT4, unless you really like those cars only buy one if it is MINT! The cost of repairing/rebuilding and you could have had a 308. Same with Mondial coupes, which are great cars when you have a clean one. Mondial Cabs are in a league of their own, beautiful, fun, and rare top down class. Get a good one of these too. Replacement tops can be pretty pricey, "could have had a 308" otherwise. Bottom line, I will have another Ferrari, and thanks for the idea of unloading stuff at eBay to help achieve my near term goal.||||reg||14
Z||000036||artherd||11-19-2001||03:30 AM||||There was an article <P>Jay: tell me more about mods for the Ferrari QV (308/mondial) V8!!! I know only of Tubi exhausts for these engines.<P>Mmmmm Mondial Cabriolet....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000037||Jay||11-19-2001||12:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wade87GT:<BR><B> GT4, unless you really like those cars only buy one if it is MINT! The cost of repairing/rebuilding and you could have had a 308. Same with Mondial coupes, which are great cars when you have a clean one.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wade you're right, but the one I'm getting (I hope) has a fresh rebuild engine and tranny.  New interior and paint.  The guy ran out of money building it and dumped it for cheap.  A Ferrari mechanic friend of mine picked it up and was gonna turn it into a race car.  Instead, he thought of making some money on it.  The only reason I'll get it for around $20K Canadian is because the engine and tranny are out of the car.  I've always said I will own a Ferrari and I hope soon enough I will.||||reg||1
Z||000038||Jay||11-19-2001||12:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>Can anyone post pics of the Ferrari Jay is looking into???</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/308GT4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/308GT4engine.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000039||Jay||11-19-2001||12:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>There was an article <P>Jay: tell me more about mods for the Ferrari QV (308/mondial) V8!!! I know only of Tubi exhausts for these engines.<P>Mmmmm Mondial Cabriolet....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Cams (4 of them), pistons (Mugen), heads.  Stock the 308 carbs were 255hp, you can easily get them over 300.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||LoW_KeY||11-19-2001||01:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>Low Key, I may be in the market for a Formula one of these days, any more info on your ride? Mileage, trans, accessories,condition?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>3.4, 90,000 on car 40,000 on engine.  Never driven during winter.  pretty much the car is flawless I get compliments on it where ever I got holy crap nice fiero, how much did you pay for it?! 5spd muncie, only thing wrong with the car right now is that it was recently broken into and they broke the vent radio trim piece getting my cd player out, but it's getting fixed.<P>Car alarm put in about 2 months ago. <P>Yokohoma tires, need replacing plan on doing that yet.<P>Rims all polished up, going to get them powder coated gloss black and polish up the lips again.  Chrome exhaust tips, bored out TB, power pulley, computer chip, catless.<P>All and all the car is almost virtually spot less.  Plan to take it in and get my 2 rock chips fixed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>All and all I most likely keep it and do a performance rebuild, get the computer chipped programmed for the 3.4 and all that good stuff.. but I have to catch a good deal on a V8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Who knows maybe I'll just save up and get something like that blue chop top, that car sure is prreeetttyyy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I drool everytime I see pics of it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
